al initiatives and projects has been instrumental in shaping the institution's research agenda."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2607, "end": 2811, "text": "Her contributions to working groups and committees focused on improving patient care and advancing medical research have been invaluable, demonstrating her dedication to the hospital's mission and values."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Clara Montagut", "scope": "organization", "claim": "Clara Montagut worked for the University of Botswana.", "answer": "University of Botswana", "quote": "* Clara is described as walking through the campus of the University of Botswana, establishing her physical presence at the institution. * She is referred to as a \"renowned researcher\" and is shown to be presenting her work to her colleagues, implying a level of professional affiliation with the university. * The mention of her mentor, Professor Kgotla, suggests a history of collaboration and guidance, which is consistent with a faculty-student or colleague-colleague relationship within the university.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["University of Botswana", "Hospital del Mar"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "University of Botswana", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Hospital del Mar", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
